ing the ones that only appear inside a bundled template.'=>'Distinct widget types in the copy, including the ones that only appear inside a bundled template.','Number of top-level elements in the copy.'=>'Number of top-level elements in the copy.','What the source site packaged.'=>'What the source site packaged.','True when a template with this title already exists on this site and will be reused instead of created.'=>'True when a template with this title already exists on this site and will be reused instead of created.','The Elementor template type (container, section, page, …).'=>'The Elementor template type (container, section, page, …).','Elementor templates the copied content renders, packaged with it. The ones missing here are created on import; the ones already here are reused untouched.'=>'Elementor templates the copied content renders, packaged with it. The ones missing here are created on import; the ones already here are reused untouched.','Widget types that import but stay inert until a Premium Addons Pro license is present.'=>'Widget types that import but stay inert until a Premium Addons Pro license is present.','Widget types not installed or deactivated here. They still import, but will not render until the widget is available.'=>'Widget types not installed or deactivated here. They still import, but will not render until the widget is available.','True when every widget in the copied content exists and is licensed here.'=>'True when every widget in the copied content exists and is licensed here.','What this site can and cannot render from the copied content.'=>'What this site can and cannot render from the copied content.','CSS custom property carrying this preset, usable as var(<name>) so the value keeps tracking the theme.'=>'CSS custom property carrying this preset, usable as var(<name>) so the value keeps tracking the theme.','Preset label shown in the editor.'=>'Preset label shown in the editor.','Preset slug.'=>'Preset slug.','Site-wide base typography.'=>'Site-wide base typography.','Styles the theme applies site-wide. Preset variables are resolved to their values, so no entry is a var() reference.'=>'Styles the theme applies site-wide. Preset variables are resolved to their values, so no entry is a var() reference.','CSS font-size value, may be a clamp() expression.'=>'CSS font-size value, may be a clamp() expression.','CSS font-family stack.'=>'CSS font-family stack.','Typography presets, split by origin.'=>'Typography presets, split by origin.','CSS gradient value.'=>'CSS gradient value.','True when the theme declares its own font families or font sizes. When false, read the Elementor kit typography with the get-global-settings ability.'=>'True when the theme declares its own font families or font sizes. When false, read the Elementor kit typography with the get-global-settings ability.','True when the active theme is a block theme.'=>'True when the active theme is a block theme.','True when the active theme ships a theme.json file. A classic theme can ship one, so this is not the same as is_block_theme.'=>'True when the active theme ships a theme.json file. A classic theme can ship one, so this is not the same as is_block_theme.','Where the theme-origin presets come from. theme_json = declared in the theme\'s theme.json file, theme_supports = declared with add_theme_support, core_defaults = the theme declares none and everything reported under the default origin comes from WordPress core. A theme that ships a theme.json file and declares its presets through add_theme_support is reported as theme_json; the values are the same either way.'=>'Where the theme-origin presets come from. theme_json = declared in the theme\'s theme.json file, theme_supports = declared with add_theme_support, core_defaults = the theme declares none and everything reported under the default origin comes from WordPress core. A theme that ships a theme.json file and declares its presets through add_theme_support is reported as 